  "version": 1,
  "description": "How text is folded before the forbidden content patterns run and before a forbidden term or hidden town is compared. It does the part of Unicode NFKC that matters here without needing a Unicode library, so Node and PHP give the same result on any host. Order: 1 remove every character in marks_and_format (Unicode categories Mn and Cf as of unicode_version, listed here so neither language consults its own Unicode tables) and in strip; 2 turn every character in spaces into a plain space; 3 replace each character listed in map, and each in an offset range, with its plain form; 4 collapse runs of spaces and trim. A character still inside reject after that is refused (text.unsupported_character): those blocks hold lookalike letters and digits this table does not fold. Code points are hexadecimal.",
